ective subspace associated with the generator coordinate method, assuming that the overlap 〈α|α′〉 is a Hilbert-Schmidt kernel in the space of weight functions. We show that the equivalence between the diagonalization of the many-body Hamiltonian in the collective subspace and the solution of the Griffin-Hill-Wheeler equation is a dynamical question which cannot be answered by kinematical considerations alone. The treatment gives a simple picture of well known misbehaviors of the generator coordinate weight functions. An application is made to the Lipkin model.\nNUCLEAR STRUCTURE Properties of generator coordinate representations. Application to a solvable model.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"APS"}}],"refereed":true,"titles":[{"title":"Properties of Griffin-Hill-Wheeler spaces"}],"external_system_identifiers":[{"schema":"OSTI","value":"7223913"},{"schema":"SPIRES","value":"SPIRES-7365985"}],"facet_author_name":["2235517_A.F.R. de Toledo Piza","2235529_E.J.V. de Passos","984020_Minori Watanabe","995880_Maria Carolina Nemes","1009037_Diogenes Galetti"],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:128597","updated":"2023-03-06T16:32:06.159250"},"curated":true,"journal_title_variants":["Phys.Rev.C","Phys. Rev. C"]},"updated":"2023-03-06T16:32:06.159250+00:00"},{"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/4503?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A4503"},"created":"1977-01-01T00:00:00+00:00","id":"4503","metadata":{"authors":[{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/036rp1748"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"de toledo p